#---
# purpose: "A value whose static type is any, passed to an extern whose parameter is integer, aborts with the function clause error an ordinary typed function raises, on every path"
# expect: abort
#---
#
# An extern is a function with one typed clause. The received 1.5 is not an
# integer, so no clause matches, exactly as for `def f(x) when is_integer(x)`.
extern "C" defp fz_op_add_ii(integer, integer) :: integer,
  raises: ArithmeticError,
  message: "bad argument in arithmetic expression"

def main() do
  send(self(), 1.5)
  receive do
    x -> dbg(fz_op_add_ii(x, 1))
  end
end
